{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1786797034,"nonce":"F8tjVPMKSTDnFupQG5mr2n0TMtM=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADORPa0Bs8AAAABM4Wmcc8AAAAG3kgGVg"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1787263232,"nonce":"fKj5NU07OFykVjPyhThE5F+HGQA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABP6BqlA","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/99#issuecomment-5362444948"},"message":"Addressed in #117 — but not as reported, so recording what was actually found.\n\n**The NaN is gone on `main`.** The repro here solves finite, and the suspected cause is not present: the DOF vector is node-major and `_bound_side_values` broadcasts with `jnp.repeat(vals, vec)`, which is the matching layout. It was repaired incidentally by #105, which rewrote the bound resolution.\n\nIt is genuinely enforced, not merely finite. With an active floor `psi(y) = -0.06 + 0.05 y` on the vector field, minimum slack is `0.0` with DOFs sitting exactly on the floor; reading the same solution component-major is infeasible by `-5.4e-3`, which is what pins the layout.\n\n**What was still missing is the coverage this issue named.** `tests/test_fem_bounds.py` covered coordinate-expression bounds on scalar fields only, so the expression x vector-field cell was correct only by accident, with nothing to stop it regressing — and the failure mode has no loud signal, since the wrong reading has the same length as the right one.\n\n#117 adds that test plus one pinning the refusal for an expression that does not reduce to one value per node.\n\nThe cross-check against `u.gap` that this issue mentions as blocked is now unblocked, but it is not in #117 — it needs a shared oracle for a flat rigid obstacle expressed both ways, which is its own piece of work.","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1787306391,"nonce":"w9qMhX8U1nLGAl/QfICPhv2q1DA=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADORPa0Bs8AAAABM4Wmcc8AAAAG8BIMFg"},"status":2}]}